<p></p>
<h1 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-BusinessContext">Business Context</h1>
<p><span style=3D"color:#0055cc;"><strong>Not to be interpreted as requirem=
ent</strong></span></p>
<p><a href=3D"/spaces/NWPI/pages/1353762177/Firm+Feature+Packages">Firm Fea=
ture Packages</a></p>
<p><a href=3D"/spaces/NWPI/pages/1040156523/Implementing+Access+Control">Im=
plementing Access Control</a></p>
<h1 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-ModelDefinition">Model Definition</h1>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Permission">Permission</h2>
<p>&lt;TBD&gt;</p>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Role">Role</h2>
<p>&lt;TBD&gt;</p>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-UserGroup">User Group</h2>
<p>&lt;TBD&gt;</p>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Resource">Resource</h2>
<p>&lt;TBD&gt;</p>
<div class=3D"rwui_tabs">
 <ul class=3D"rwui_tabs_menu">
  <!-- These will be generated by the js -->
 </ul><!-- Here will the tabs go -->
 <div class=3D"rwui_tab_content" data-name=3D"Transition" data-hash=3D"tab-=
Transition">
  <h2 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-FeaturePackageTemplate">Feature Package Te=
mplate</h2>
  <p>Its a grouping of <strong>one</strong> User Group and zero or more Res=
ources.</p>
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Types">Types</h3>
  <ul>
   <li>Firm - Builds packages assigned to firms</li>
   <li>User - Builds packages assigned to users</li>
  </ul>
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Attributes">Attributes</h3>
  <ol>
   <li>Feature package must include one and only one User Group</li>
   <li>In a firm package, a resource inclusion can be marked option (add-on=
) and in addition specified to be included by default in an assignment to a=
 firm.</li>
   <li>User package templates don't have add-ons</li>
  </ol>
  <h2 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-FeaturePackage">Feature Package</h2>
  <p>It's the assignment of package template to a user or firm.</p>
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Attributes.1">Attributes</h3>
  <ol>
   <li>Firm assignment can optionally select/unselect any add-on resource i=
n the package template</li>
  </ol>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"rwui_tab_content" data-name=3D"Target" data-hash=3D"tab-Targ=
et">
  <h2 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Feature">Feature</h2>
  <p>Features represent the units of value within the platform, expressed f=
rom the perspective of the buyers of firms. Features can represent any prod=
uct or service that &nbsp;is being offered to the firm when they decide to =
buy or upgrade to compass x.</p>
  <p>These features can be associated with digital features or services and=
 can be used to monitor/manage access to feature versions and usage levels.=
</p>
  <p>Technically, feature represents a business functionality/operation. It=
's an aggregate of technical role/permission <strong>and/or</strong> techni=
cal resources under IAM.</p>
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Attributes.2">Attributes</h3>
  <ol>
   <li>Feature may have a strong association with one or many firm configur=
ation attributes. When such relationship exists, the feature package must r=
espect it and ensure its within the bounds of it's own associations</li>
   <li>Feature includes versioning and only one feature version can be incl=
uded in a feature package <sub><em>(Feature Package are explained in detail=
, further in this article)</em></sub></li>
   <li>Feature may be dependent on another feature</li>
   <li>Feature may be incomplete and un-assignable unless they are assigned=
 together with another feature variation from the same group</li>
  </ol>
  <h2 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-FeaturePackage.1">Feature Package</h2>
  <p>Its a grouping of features via feature groups.</p>
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Attributes.3">Attributes</h3>
  <ol>
   <li>Feature package may have a strong association with one or many firm =
configuration attributes. When such relationship exists, the feature packag=
e must ensure all included features are within the bounds of it's own assoc=
iations</li>
   <li>Feature package includes versioning and only one version can be assi=
gned to a firm or user</li>
  </ol>
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-FirmPackage">Firm Package</h3>
  <p>Packages assigned to firms via their firm configuration.</p>
  <h4 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Add-On">Add-On</h4>
  <p>The association of a Feature in a package may optionally mark this rel=
ationship as an add-on. This exempts this feature to be automatically assig=
ned to the firm via the package assignment, while this feature would have t=
o be included <u>explicitly</u> during the assignment.</p>
  <h4 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Quota">Quota</h4>
  <p>The association of a Feature in a package may also define the usage li=
mits. This would apply at the firm level, upon its assignment to a firm.&nb=
sp;</p>
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-UserPackage">User Package</h3>
  <p>Packages assigned to users.</p>
 </div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-ConfigurationManagement">Configuration Manag=
ement</h2>
<p>Configuration management will be access controlled with Okta scopes usin=
g a REST interface.&nbsp;</p>
<h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-UserGroup.1">User Group</h3>
<ol>
 <li>Create -(UG5)</li>
 <li>Remove (UG6)=20
  <ol>
   <li>remove if there are no role/user associations</li>
  </ol></li>
 <li>update attributes (PUT)&nbsp; (UG7)</li>
 <li>update - add/remove roles (UG3 UG4)&nbsp;</li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Role.1">Role</h3>
<ol>
 <li>Create (R1)</li>
 <li>Remove (R2)=20
  <ol>
   <li>remove if there are no user group/permission associations</li>
  </ol></li>
 <li>update - add/remove permissions (<span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">R3)</s=
pan></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Permission.1">Permission</h3>
<ol>
 <li>Create (P1)</li>
 <li>Remove (P2)&nbsp;=20
  <ol>
   <li>remove if there are no role associations</li>
  </ol></li>
 <li>activate/de-activate (<span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">P6)</span></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Resource.1">Resource</h3>
<ol>
 <li>Create (G1)</li>
 <li>Remove (G2)=20
  <ol>
   <li>remove if there are no user/package template associations</li>
  </ol></li>
 <li><s>update attributes - name and description (PUT) (G14)</s></li>
 <li>
  <p>activate/de-activate (<span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">G11)&nbsp;</span>=
</p></li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
<div class=3D"rwui_tabs">
 <ul class=3D"rwui_tabs_menu">
  <!-- These will be generated by the js -->
 </ul><!-- Here will the tabs go -->
 <div class=3D"rwui_tab_content" data-name=3D"Transition" data-hash=3D"tab-=
Transition">
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-FeaturePackageTemplate.1">Feature Package =
Template</h3>
  <ol>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Create (<strong>PT1</strong>)</span>
    <ol>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">create package template and add des=
cription</span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">choose the package type from F (fir=
m) or U (user)</span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">For firm package, assign firm type<=
/span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">set active =3D true</span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">create associations</span>
      <ol>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">can be associated with multiple e=
xisting resources (by name and type)</span>
        <ol>
         <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">define if the resource associat=
ion is an add-on</span></li>
         <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">define if it should be selected=
 by default</span></li>
        </ol></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Only for User package templates -=
 must be associated with one existing user group (by name)</span></li>
      </ol></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">update - name and description&nbsp; (=
<strong>PT3</strong>)</span></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">activate/de-activate (<strong>PT3</st=
rong>)</span></li>
   <li>Remove (<strong>PT4</strong>)=20
    <ol>
     <li>remove if there are no associations with a package</li>
    </ol></li>
  </ol>
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-FeaturePackage.2">Feature Package</h3>
  <ol>
   <li>Create (<strong>PK1</strong>)=20
    <ol>
     <li>create feature package and add description</li>
     <li>link the package template id</li>
     <li>set version =3D 1 and active =3D true&nbsp;</li>
     <li>Add package assignments. For each assignment=20
      <ol>
       <li>link template assignment id</li>
       <li>set active true for selected add-on or included or false for uns=
elected add-on</li>
       <li><u>ensure</u> template assignment id has the same template id as=
 linked with the package</li>
       <li><u>ensure</u> <strong>included</strong> assignment in template a=
ssignment is being set to true</li>
       <li>ensure all template assignments are included in the request</li>
      </ol></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li>Remove (<strong>PK3</strong>)=20
    <ol>
     <li>remove if there are no associations with a firm/user</li>
    </ol></li>
   <li>Update (<strong>PK5</strong>)=20
    <ol>
     <li>update package assignments</li>
    </ol></li>
  </ol>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"rwui_tab_content" data-name=3D"Target" data-hash=3D"tab-Targ=
et">
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-Feature.1"><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">=
Feature</span></h3>
  <ul>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">creation</span>
    <ol>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">create feature and add description<=
/span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">configure quota (usage limit) <u>ap=
plicability</u></span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">create firm configuration criteria =
(query)</span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">create a new feature version</span>=
</li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">define transitive feature dependenc=
ies (if any)</span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">define feature variation dependenci=
es (if any)</span></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">update</span>
    <ol>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">name and description update</span><=
/li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Any other update will result in cre=
ation of a new version&nbsp;</span></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">view</span></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">archiving</span>
    <ul>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">soft delete</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Archiving will put the feature in=
 an inactive state. This feature will be omitted from all use-cases except =
view by name+version, id or search with inactive state</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">A feature can't be archived until=
 it's referenced in any active feature package via any feature group</span>=
</li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Inactive features can't be activa=
ted</span></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">removing</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Inactive features after 'X' days =
can be permanently removed</span></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul></li>
  </ul>
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-FeatureGroup"><span style=3D"color:#c9372c=
;">Feature Group</span></h3>
  <ul>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">creation</span>
    <ol>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">create feature group and add descri=
ption</span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">define selection type (select one o=
r many)</span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">add features to the group. ensure a=
ddition of feature variation(s) when a dependent feature is defined</span>
      <ol>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">ensure only one version of a feat=
ure is included</span></li>
      </ol></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">create a new feature group version<=
/span></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">update</span>
    <ol>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">name and description update</span><=
/li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Any other update will result in cre=
ation of a new version</span></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">view</span></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">archiving</span>
    <ul>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">soft delete</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Archiving will put the feature gr=
oup in an inactive state. This feature group will be omitted from all use-c=
ases except view by name+version, id or search with inactive state</span></=
li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">A feature group can't be archived=
 until it's referenced in any active feature package</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Inactive feature group can't be a=
ctivated</span></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">removing</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Inactive feature group after 'X' =
days can be permanently removed</span></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul></li>
  </ul>
  <h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-FeaturePackage.3"><span style=3D"color:#c9=
372c;">Feature Package</span></h3>
  <ol>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">creation</span>
    <ol>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">create feature package and add desc=
ription</span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">link the package template id</span>=
</li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">set version =3D 1 and active =3D tr=
ue</span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Add package assignments. For each a=
ssignment</span>
      <ol>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">link template assignment id</span=
></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">set active true for selected add-=
on or included or false for unselected add-on</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;"><u>ensure</u> template assignment=
 id has the same template id as linked with the package</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;"><u>ensure</u> included assignment=
 in template assignment is being set to true</span></li>
      </ol></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">update</span>
    <ol>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">name and description update</span><=
/li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">add/remove feature groups or any ot=
her change will result in creation of a new feature package and auto-upgrad=
e to this new version for assigned firm/user at a specific datetime</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">The previous version will be mark=
ed for expiry at that datetime</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">The new version will be effective=
 from that datetime&nbsp;</span></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">view</span></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">archiving</span>
    <ol>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">soft delete</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Archiving will put the feature pa=
ckage in an inactive state. This feature package will be omitted from all u=
se-cases except view by name+version, id or search with inactive state</spa=
n></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">A feature package can't be archiv=
ed until it's assigned to a firm/user</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Inactive feature package can't be=
 activated</span></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">removing</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Inactive feature package after 'X=
' days can be permanently removed</span></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">assignment</span>
    <ol>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Firm</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">The previous version of an associ=
ated package will be marked for expiry at the defined datetime</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">The new version or package associ=
ation will be effective from a defined datetime&nbsp;</span></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">User</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">The previous version of an associ=
ated package will be marked for expiry at the defined datetime</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">The new version or package associ=
ation will be effective from a defined datetime&nbsp;</span></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Apply feature updates</span>
    <ol>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Assignment would lead to refresh of=
 access control for users</span>
      <ol>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Firm package update</span>
        <ol>
         <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Find all the users of this Firm=
</span></li>
        </ol></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Association of a new firm package=
 to a firm would result in ...</span></li>
      </ol></li>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">User package update</span></li>
    </ol></li>
  </ol>
 </div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"FeatureConfiguration-AccessControlAssignment">Access Control Assi=
gnment</h3>
